# Pairs with RestoredCutNotReAdvanced. The resume that starts replication
# below the restored frontier: after the restore, a shipper whose alias-change
# push was lost keeps shipping from the retired copy's log until its backstop
# re-resolve, so a pre-restore write still unshipped there reaches the peer's
# restored copy. This was production's gate before the #4490 fix (#4498): the
# shipper re-checked its binding only on the push or after
# ShipSourceIdentityBackstopInterval. Its code analogue (a resume that leaves
# the identity-resolved flag set) turns the regression test red.
MODULE: RestoredCutNotReAdvancedResumeShipsRetiredLog
TARGET: RestoredCutNotReAdvanced
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: shipping resumes from the retired copy's log when the rebind push was lost
PERTURBS: Ship

--- FIND
    /\ recvOn[Peer(c)]
    /\ bound[c] = alias[c]
--- REPLACE
    /\ recvOn[Peer(c)]
    \* MUTATION: no re-resolve before shipping.
--- END
